<title>USA: U.S. Q3 corporate profits fell 2.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q3 corporate profits fell 2.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department preliminary estimates of third quarter profits by U.S. corporations, with comparisons. Profits before tax include inventory valuation and capital consumption adjustments.</p>
<p>Data are chain weighted and expressed in seasonally adjusted annual rates of billions of dollars, with third quarter percent changes from the second quarter.</p>
<p> -		  Pct--Q3'96-P  Q2'96--Rev from---1995</p>
<p> -  After Tax  -2.6  397.5    408.1    408.1   380.2</p>
<p> -  Before Tax -0.2  654.7    655.8    655.8   586.6</p>
<p> Tax Liability -2.1  231.4    236.4    236.4   218.7</p>
</text>
